Description: Peek at a window from its preview in the taskbar pop-up
 Like Windows 11: resting the pointer on a window's preview for 300 ms brings
 that window to the front (un-minimising it if needed). Moving to another
 preview peeks that one instead and puts a peeked minimised window back down.
 Leaving the pop-up, or it closing, without a click activates the window that
 was active before and minimises the peeked window again if it was minimised.
 A click keeps the window and closes the pop-up.
 .
 The pop-up stays open while the pointer is on it: a peeked window that the
 window manager raises over the pop-up (an unmanaged window) no longer counts
 as the pointer leaving, the pop-up is raised back on top, and moving onto a
 preview inside the pop-up (an "inferior" crossing) is not a leave either.
 A peek belongs to the pop-up it started in, because docklike hides every
 other button's pop-up whenever one opens.
Author: KiteOS <6760806+iwankurnia@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
